.TH BLS 1 "July 2026" "bless 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bls \- command shorthand for bless, a small Ghostty-oriented pager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bls
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I FILE
.br
.I COMMAND
.B | bls -
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bless
is a terminal pager inspired by
.BR less (1).
It renders directly to a modern Ghostty-compatible terminal and uses
.B libghostty-vt
for SGR parsing so coloured command output can be preserved.
.PP
The installed command is
.B bls
to avoid conflicting with Apple macOS' built-in
.BR bless (8)
utility while keeping the program name
.BR bless .
.PP
.B bless
does not read standard input implicitly when no file is given. Use
.B -
as the file operand to read from standard input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ,\  --help
Display help and exit.
.SH OPERANDS
.TP
.I FILE
The file to view. Use
.B -
to read from standard input.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR q ,\  Esc ,\  Ctrl-C
Quit.
.TP
.BR j ,\  Down
Scroll down one line.
.TP
.BR k ,\  Up
Scroll up one line.
.TP
.BR Space ,\  d ,\  PageDown
Scroll down half a page.
.TP
.BR u ,\  PageUp
Scroll up half a page.
.TP
.BR g
Go to the first page.
.TP
.BR G
Go to the last page.
.TP
.BR h ,\  Left
Scroll left.
.TP
.BR l ,\  Right
Scroll right.
.TP
.B /
Search.
.TP
.BR n ,\  N
Go to the next or previous search match.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BLESS_MAX_BYTES
Maximum number of bytes to load. The default is 256MiB. Values may use
.BR B ,
.BR KiB ,
.BR MiB ,
or
.BR GiB
suffixes.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
View a file:
.B bls Cargo.toml
.TP
View coloured command output:
.B fastfetch --pipe false | bls -
.TP
Raise the load cap:
.B BLESS_MAX_BYTES=1GiB bls huge.log
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR less (1),
.BR ghostty (1)
